# Issues: #149, #177

Feature: First-Class Epic Support and Multi-PR Delivery Flow
  As an nmg-sdlc plugin maintainer (interactive) and as the SDLC runner (automated)
  I want the SDLC to natively handle features that span multiple PRs
  So that I never have to improvise coordination structures on top of the pipeline

  # --- /draft-issue: Epic classification and body format ---

  # --- /write-spec: parent-link resolution ---

  # --- /write-spec: seal-spec flow ---

  # --- /open-pr: sibling-aware bumping ---

  # --- sdlc-runner: topological ordering ---

  # --- Unattended-mode determinism for all new gates ---

  # --- Issue #177: coordination-only epic lifecycle supersession ---

  @SCN024
  Scenario: Automatic discovery excludes epics before filling the shortlist
    Given a milestone contains a confirmed epic, ready ordinary issues, and ready epic children
    When start-issue builds and backfills its selectable shortlist
    Then the confirmed epic is excluded before the target choice count is evaluated
    And the ready ordinary issues and children remain selectable under normal dependency rules

  @SCN025
  Scenario: An explicit epic start returns ready children without mutation
    Given issue #E is a confirmed epic with at least one ready child
    When the user explicitly invokes start-issue for #E
    Then no branch is created or checked out
    And no issue or Project status is changed
    And the response explains that #E is coordination-only and presents its ready children

  @SCN026
  Scenario: Nested epic lineage is informational only
    Given ready child #C belongs to nested epic #N whose parent is epic #R
    And #C has one genuine execution dependency that is closed
    When start-issue renders and evaluates #C
    Then it shows lineage #R then #N with both issue numbers and titles
    And neither epic contributes a blocking edge or topological in-degree
    And the genuine dependency retains its ordinary readiness semantics

  @SCN027
  Scenario: The first child creates separate aggregate and executable specs
    Given confirmed epic #E has no canonical aggregate and ready child #C enters write-spec
    When all requirements, design, tasks, and publication gates are approved
    Then an epic aggregate package is created without tasks or Gherkin
    And a separate five-file executable child package plus epic-link is created for #C
    And the exact approved spec set becomes canonical without starting or closing #E

  @SCN028
  Scenario: Aggregate and child authority is unique and bidirectional
    Given an epic aggregate and linked child packages have been authored
    When epic specification authority is validated
    Then aggregate EO outcomes and topology have no executable ownership
    And every executable AC, FR, task, and scenario has exactly one child issue owner
    And epic-scope and every epic-link agree on issue, path, and outcome mappings

  @SCN029
  Scenario: A later child receives an independent package
    Given epic #E has a canonical aggregate and an existing child package
    And later ready child #L enters write-spec
    When #L's reviewed specification is approved
    Then #L receives its own linked executable package
    And only #L's planned aggregate entry is updated
    And existing aggregate prose and sibling packages remain unchanged unless separately approved

  @SCN030
  Scenario: Open-pr remains active while delivery is remediable
    Given a verified child has an open pull request with pending checks or actionable review findings
    When open-pr observes the delivery
    Then it monitors pending checks and safely fixes actionable findings
    And it reverifies and pushes each changed head before observing again
    And it does not report lifecycle completion while the pull request remains unmerged

  @SCN031
  Scenario: Open-pr merges only the exact clean verified head
    Given all configured checks for the current head are success-equivalent
    And requested changes and actionable unresolved threads are absent
    And the live mergeStateStatus is CLEAN
    When open-pr completes delivery
    Then it revalidates and merges that exact head
    And it proves the pull request is MERGED and the child issue is CLOSED before success

  @SCN032
  Scenario: Closing the final child closes its eligible epic
    Given a merged child is closed and every fully paged native sibling is closed
    And aggregate and child specification authority is valid
    When post-merge epic completion runs
    Then the epic's readable Project status is reconciled to Done
    And the epic is explicitly closed and both resulting states are re-fetched

  @SCN033
  Scenario: Nested closure cascades and unverifiable graphs stop safely
    Given an eligible inner epic is itself a child of an outer epic
    When the inner epic closes
    Then completion is re-evaluated leaf-to-root until an incomplete parent is reached
    But a cycle, incomplete page, zero-child epic, unresolved child, conflicting identity, spec gap, or unreadable required state stops mutation with exact evidence

  @SCN034
  Scenario: Upgrade-project repairs one explicitly approved epic at a time
    Given upgrade-project finds legacy spec ownership, relationship drift, or stale epic state
    When it renders a per-epic proposal and the user approves that exact digest
    Then the workflow revalidates drift and applies only the approved spec and GitHub mutations
    And ambiguous ownership remains unchanged and is routed to an explicit child-drafting decision
    And post-apply proof plus a repeated audit demonstrates idempotence

  @SCN035
  Scenario: Documentation and distributed templates share the runtime contract
    Given the coordination-only epic lifecycle is implemented
    When repository documentation, managed generators, and distributed templates are audited
    Then README and contribution guidance explain selection, lineage, split authority, terminal delivery, closure, and repair
    And onboarding, upgrade, write-spec, issue-form, contribution-gate, and steering assets agree
    And contract and disposable-repository exercises reject lifecycle drift
